title: $:/plugins/wikilabs/devtools/history


V 0.8.0 - 2026.09.19

* Source position tracking runs on a module shared with tw-mcp-core, so the browser view and the MCP tools trace every element to the same lines with the same code.
* Line numbers follow edits to a tiddler instead of waiting for tracking to be switched off and on again.
* Content from a procedure or macro defined in the same tiddler points at its lines in that tiddler, where it showed the procedure's name and line 1.

V 0.7.1 - 2026.09.19

* The settings say that source position tracking applies at once to content rendered afterwards; a reload is only needed to trace what is already on screen.

V 0.7.0 - 2026.09.17

* Source position tracking now also records which variable produced a subtree, and its line helpers moved to `utils.js` so other plugins can share them.
* On a server the tooltip, context menu, source viewer, inline editor and variable inspector are no longer loaded at all.
* Source position tracking now starts switched OFF, as the readme always said it did. Switch it on in Control Panel → Settings → WikiLabs.

V 0.6.1 - 2026.05.09

* Fix startup ordering so `$tw.popup` exists when the click-handler runs (regression exposed by TW core PR #9305).

V 0.6.0 - 2026.04.10

* Rename DOM attributes: `data-source-pos` → `data-pos`, `data-source-start`+`data-source-end` → `data-range`, `data-source-context` → `data-ctx`, `data-source-caller` → `data-caller`

V 0.5.0 - 2026.03.31

* initial release
* name: devtools
